arts as an overwhelming favorite regardless of the national climate.", "watch": "Emerging state polling showing single digits, or a historically large national Democratic wave, would be the main signals that Wyoming could tighten.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming is the most Republican-leaning state in the country, with a presidential partisan lean of roughly 23 points toward Republicans. With the incumbent term-limited, both parties will nominate new candidates, but the state's underlying partisanship dominates the picture. No public polls of the race or expert ratings are available, so the state's fundamental lean drives the outlook.\n\nNational headlines point to a difficult environment for the party holding the White House, and Democrats have gained ground in other races this cycle. Even so, Wyoming's presidential margin has been exceptionally stable across recent cycles, and a shift large enough to put the state in play would be historically unprecedented. The Republican nominee is a strong favorite, and the real uncertainty is the size of the winning margin rather than the winner's identity.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0279, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0258, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.020